      "name": null,
      "problem": "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{5-x}{3}=7x-15.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-x}{3} & =7x-15 \\\\ 3(\\frac{5-x}{3}) & =3(7x-15) \\\\ \\cancel{3}(\\frac{5-x}{\\cancel{3}}) & =21x-45 \\\\ 5-x & =21x-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-x & =21x-45 \\\\ 5-x+x & =21x-45+x \\\\ 5 & =22x-45 \\\\ 5+45 & =22x-45+45 \\\\ 50 & =22x \\\\ \\frac{50}{22} & =\\frac{22x}{22} \\\\ \\frac{25}{11} & =\\frac{\\cancel{22}x}{\\cancel{22}} \\\\ x & =\\frac{25}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
