      "problem": "Solve the equation $\\frac{8y+5}{3}=6y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8y+5}{3} & =6y \\\\ 3(\\frac{8y+5}{3}) & =3\\cdot 6y \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{8y+5}{\\cancel{3}}) & =18y \\\\ 8y+5 & =18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8y+5 & =18y \\\\ 8y+5-8y & =18y-8y \\\\ 5 & =10y \\\\ \\frac{5}{10} & =\\frac{10y}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
