      "problem": "Solve for $t$ where $-2t=\\frac{4-6t}{9}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $9$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2t & =\\frac{4-6t}{9} \\\\ \\frac{4-6t}{9} & =-2t \\\\ 9(\\frac{4-6t}{9}) & =9(-2t) \\\\ \\cancel{9}(\\frac{4-6t}{\\cancel{9}}) & =-18t \\\\ 4-6t & =-18t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-6t & =-18t \\\\ 4-6t+6t & =-18t+6t \\\\ 4 & =-12t \\\\ -12t & =4 \\\\ \\frac{-12t}{-12} & =\\frac{4}{-12} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-12}t}{\\cancel{-12}} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ t & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
