      "problem": "If $\\frac{3k-2}{6}=-(k+2),$ then $k=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $6$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3k-2}{6} & =-(k+2) \\\\ 6\\cdot (\\frac{3k-2}{6}) & =6\\cdot (-(k+2)) \\\\ \\cancel{6}\\cdot (\\frac{3k-2}{\\cancel{6}}) & =-6(k+2) \\\\ 3k-2 & =-6k-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k-2 & =-6k-12 \\\\ 3k-2+6k & =-6k-12+6k \\\\ 9k-2 & =-12 \\\\ 9k-2+2 & =-12+2 \\\\ 9k & =-10 \\\\ \\frac{9k}{9} & =\\frac{-10}{9} \\\\ k & =-\\frac{10}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
